# Go organization

## Layout

- `pkg/` — shared libraries (schema, fsutil). No `internal/` here; importable by agent and cli.
- `agent/internal/` — agent-only code. Group by domain, one concern per package.
- `cli/internal/` — cli-only code, same rules.
- Name files by role: `auth/token.go`, `deploy/store.go`, `api/deploy/handler.go` — not `utils.go` or `helpers.go`.

## File size

- **Hard cap: 500 lines per file.** Before approaching it, extract to a sibling file in the same package or to `pkg/` if shared.
- Prefer many small files over few large ones.

## Packages

- `main` only in `cmd/*/main.go` — thin: load config, wire deps, run.
- HTTP handlers live under `agent/internal/api/<resource>/`.
- Business logic in domain packages (`deploy`, `auth`, `secret`) — handlers call into them.

## Imports

- Standard library, blank line, third party, blank line, `github.com/awade12/hanager-deploy/...`.
- No circular imports; push shared types to `pkg/schema`.

## Errors

- Wrap with `%w`; domain packages define typed errors in `errors.go`.
- Return validation errors as structured lists, not opaque strings.

## Tests

- Table-driven tests; fixtures in `testdata/` next to the package.
- `_test.go` files stay with the code they test.
